dialect protocol
protocol stdio.semio.snapshot
version 1
schema stdio.semio
start body
framing record

# W-S closer (`any`): REAL binary pack frame, replacing the old `serde_json::to_vec`-in-envelope
# shortcut. `format u8` + `tag u8` (real subset ordinal, `📸️snapshot/🦀️component.rs`'s
# `subset_ordinal`) are genuinely, individually protocol-walkable, then `schema_len`/`schema_bytes`
# (real, varint-length-prefixed UTF-8 — this envelope's own top-level `schema` field). Past that,
# `payload` is the WRAPPED subset's own full, already-real `ArtifactPack::encode_pack()` output —
# a real nested `semio_format` envelope in its own right — modeled as one opaque trailing chain
# (the `protocol-array-of-records`/`protocol-prim-ref-recursion` gap: one-of-13 heterogeneous
# nested payloads can't be tag-dispatched by `repeat`, which only dispatches WITHIN one block, not
# across an entire independent sub-protocol). The real Rust `encode_semio_snapshot_binary`/
# `decode_semio_snapshot_binary` stays genuinely delegating; only the protocol DESCRIPTION stops at
# this boundary, same honest treatment every P1-P3 pilot's own nested payload uses.
header fixed 2
field format u8
field tag u8

segment schema_len varint
segment schema_bytes Array(u8, Field(schema_len))

chain payload bytes
